Cursor carries `created_at::text`, not the JS `Date`: `pg` parses timestamps to millisecond `Date`s, Postgres stores microseconds → a truncated cursor skips or repeats rows at page boundaries.

Needs a matching index, or every page sorts the whole table: `CREATE INDEX ON orders (created_at DESC, id DESC);`

Newest first, `limit` default 20, clamped to 1–100; `next_cursor: null` = last page.

